{"title":"1970 AHSME Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A square and a circle have equal perimeters. The ratio of the area of the circle to the area of the square is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/3/ed3d13ffe032d4ebc75710f58ddf6bbb10c0f3b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) } \\frac{4}{\\pi}\\quad \\text{(B) } \\frac{\\pi}{\\sqrt{2}}\\quad \\text{(C) } \\frac{4}{1}\\quad \\text{(D) } \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\pi}\\quad \\text{(E) } \\frac{\\pi}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"317\" height=\"45\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let's say the circle has a circumference ( or perimeter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/2/a72a1caa0cb9e0f72f414ebd8180ea676808568f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" />). Since the perimeter of the square is the same as the perimeter of the circle, the side length of the square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" />. That means that the area of the square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/4/0a490286316c84d1b6016469f9e03bee57ed7d67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi^2$\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" />. The area of the circle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/2/a72a1caa0cb9e0f72f414ebd8180ea676808568f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" />. So the area of the circle over the area of the square is  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/c/1bc4840d6ae3fdf27940cbb8644d5c0d8d0ba765.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4\\pi}{\\pi^2} \\Rightarrow \\frac{4}{\\pi} \\Rightarrow$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"90\" height=\"37\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/6/386255c1da145bc497cf598169ccbaa210e8d0cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"24\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_AHSME\" title=\"1970 AHSME\">1970 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1970 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1970 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1970\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1970 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by